  "final_answer_preview": "A person who unlawfully or negligently does any act that is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life can be punished under Section 271 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023. This section specifies that such conduct can lead to imprisonment for up to six months, a fine, or both. Additionally, Section 270 also addresses negligent acts likely to spread infection, categorizing them as public nuisances, which may also apply.",
